I’ve built a standalone CLI that uses the lightweight, browser‑free core from `deepterm` (including its WASM‑based PoW solver) and combines it with your existing features: session management, file upload, chat history, multi‑line interactive input, and automatic retry on “server busy” errors. No Puppeteer required – just Node.js, `form-data`, and the `deepseek.wasm` file.

Save it as `dslight.mjs` in `~/deepseek-cli` and run it with:

```bash
export DEEPSEEK_TOKEN="Bearer ey..."   # your token
node dslight.mjs -i                    # interactive session
